{
 "id": 7,
 "number": 36,
 "title": "Valid Sudoku",
 "slug": "valid-sudoku",
 "category": "arrays-hashing",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/valid-sudoku/",
 "pattern": "One hash set of row / column / box facts",
 "statement": "Decide whether a partly filled 9×9 Sudoku board is **valid so far**: no digit may repeat within a row, within a column, or within any of the nine 3×3 boxes. Empty cells are `.` and are ignored. (The board does not have to be solvable.)",
 "example": {
  "input": "board = [[\"8\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n         [\"6\",\".\",\".\",\"1\",\"9\",\"5\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n         [\".\",\"9\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\"],\n         [\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"3\"],\n         [\"4\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"1\"],\n         [\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\"],\n         [\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\"8\",\".\"],\n         [\".\",\".\",\".\",\"4\",\"1\",\"9\",\".\",\".\",\"5\"],\n         [\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\"9\"]]",
  "output": "False",
  "why": "There are two 8s in the top-left 3×3 box: at (0, 0) and at (2, 2)."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "board = [[\"5\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n         [\"6\",\".\",\".\",\"1\",\"9\",\"5\",\".\",\".\",\".\"],\n         [\".\",\"9\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\"],\n         [\"8\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"3\"],\n         [\"4\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\"3\",\".\",\".\",\"1\"],\n         [\"7\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"6\"],\n         [\".\",\"6\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"2\",\"8\",\".\"],\n         [\".\",\".\",\".\",\"4\",\"1\",\"9\",\".\",\".\",\"5\"],\n         [\".\",\".\",\".\",\".\",\"8\",\".\",\".\",\"7\",\"9\"]]",
   "output": "True"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Each filled cell must be unique in three places at once: its row, its column and its 3×3 box.",
  "Turn that into three *facts* per digit — **row r has d**, **column c has d**, **box b has d** — and keep all facts in one hash set. The box of cell (r, c) is (r // 3, c // 3).",
  "Scan the board once. If any of a digit's three facts is already in the set, the board is invalid. Otherwise add the three facts and continue."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def isValidSudoku(self, board: List[List[str]]) -> bool:\n        seen = set()\n\n        for i in range(9):\n            for j in range(9):\n                if board[i][j] != \".\":\n                    num = board[i][j]\n                    if (\n                        (i, num) in seen\n                        or (num, j) in seen\n                        or (i // 3, j // 3, num) in seen\n                    ):\n                        return False\n                    seen.add((i, num))\n                    seen.add((num, j))\n                    seen.add((i // 3, j // 3, num))\n\n        return True",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(1)",
  "timeWhy": "The board is always 9×9 = 81 cells, each checked with three O(1) set lookups.",
  "space": "O(1)",
  "spaceWhy": "At most 3 facts for each of the 81 cells."
 },
